{
  "id": "open-source-infrastructure",
  "title": "Critical open-source infrastructure",
  "summary": "Security and maintenance funding for 18 open-source projects much of the internet runs on, from curl and OpenSSL to zlib and XZ Utils, using Debian dependents, OSV.dev CVE history and GitHub maintainer activity as of November 2026. The projects are real; funding needs and costs are illustrative, and no project asked for this money.",
  "valueUnit": "maintainer-weeks of security work per $10,000",
  "sources": [
    {
      "name": "Debian 13 (trixie) main/amd64 package index",
      "url": "https://deb.debian.org/debian/dists/trixie/main/binary-amd64/Packages.xz"
    },
    {
      "name": "OSV.dev vulnerability database (Debian ecosystem)",
      "url": "https://osv.dev/"
    },
    {
      "name": "GitHub REST API: repository commits and languages",
      "url": "https://docs.github.com/en/rest/commits/commits"
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": {
    "maintainer_year_usd": 200000,
    "audit_usd": 100000,
    "cap_rule": "audit + maintainer-years = max(1, sqrt(MB of code on GitHub)), rounded to $10k",
    "urgency_multiples": [
      2.0,
      1.4,
      0.8,
      0.4
    ],
    "urgency_breakpoints": [
      0,
      0.25,
      0.6,
      1.0
    ],
    "note": "Projects and data are real (Debian 13 package index, OSV.dev and GitHub, retrieved 2026-11-11); costs and needs are illustrative, and no project asked for this money. A maintainer-year costs $200,000 fully loaded, so $10,000 buys 2.6 maintainer-weeks. Each project's cap is one $100,000 security audit plus max(1, sqrt(MB of source code)) maintainer-years, so bigger codebases can absorb more but not proportionally more. The first quarter of the cap (audit, fuzzing, urgent fixes) is worth 2x a routine week, falling to 1.4x at 25%, 0.8x at 60% and 0.4x at the cap. Reach is direct dependents among Debian packages, which undercounts tools (OpenSSH, sudo) and code used mainly via npm/PyPI/Maven. Security exposure counts CVEs Debian tracked against the project since 2016-11-11, which partly reflects how carefully a project files CVEs (curl files many), not only how buggy it is. Core contributors are people with 12+ non-merge, non-bot commits on the default branch from 2025-11-11 to 2026-11-11; mirrors (libxml2, GnuPG, SQLite) and multiple identities make this approximate. Lens weights: Reach = sqrt(dependents / median); Security exposure = sqrt(CVEs / median) x (dependents / median)^0.25; Maintainer fragility = sqrt(dependents / median) x sqrt(top author share / median) / sqrt(core contributors). Funders are fictional."
  },
